{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"83","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. Track"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"5 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You already know that Valery's favorite sport is biathlon. Due to your help, he learned to shoot without missing, and his skills are unmatched at the shooting range. But now a smaller task is to be performed, he should learn to complete the path fastest."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The track's map is represented by a rectangle "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n × m"},{"kind":"text","text":" in size divided into squares. Each square is marked with a lowercase Latin letter (which means the type of the plot), with the exception of the starting square (it is marked with a capital Latin letters "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":") and the terminating square (it is marked with a capital Latin letter "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":"). The time of movement from one square to another is equal to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1"},{"kind":"text","text":" minute. The time of movement within the cell can be neglected. We can move from the cell only to side-adjacent ones, but it is forbidden to go beyond the map edges. Also the following restriction is imposed on the path: it is not allowed to visit more than "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"different types"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of squares (squares of one type can be visited an infinite number of times). Squares marked with "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" have no type, so they are not counted. But "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be visited exactly once — at the very beginning, and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" must be visited exactly once — at the very end."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to find the path from the square "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" to the square "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" that takes minimum time. Among all shortest paths you should choose the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"lexicographically minimal"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" one. When comparing paths you should lexicographically represent them as a sequence of characters, that is, of plot types."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first input line contains three integers "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"k"},{"kind":"text","text":" ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"1 ≤ n, m ≤ 50, n·m ≥ 2, 1 ≤ k ≤ 4"},{"kind":"text","text":"). Then "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contain the map. Each line has the length of exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"m"},{"kind":"text","text":" characters and consists of lowercase Latin letters and characters "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":". It is guaranteed that the map contains exactly one character "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" and exactly one character "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Pretest 12 is one of the maximal tests for this problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there is a path that satisfies the condition, print it as a sequence of letters — the plot types. Otherwise, print \"-1\" (without quotes). "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You shouldn't print the character "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"S"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the beginning and "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"T"},{"kind":"text","text":" in the end"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that this sequence may be empty."}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" This case is present in pretests. You can just print nothing or print one \"End of line\"-character. Both will be accepted."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 3 2\nSba\nccc\naac\nccc\nabT\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"bcccc\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3 4 1\nSxyy\nyxxx\nyyyT\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"xxxx\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 3 3\nTyS\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"y\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1 4 1\nSxyT\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"-1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"83C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/83/problem/C"}